      "content": "The point isn't to pretend—it's to stop performing for an audience that's already left the theater. You're not dragging a broken thing; you're carrying a corpse that you keep insisting is still you. Let it rot where it belongs, and let the silence after the noise be the only thing you owe anyone. If you can't become something new yet, then just be nothing for a while—that's still a kind of living.",
